 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Say hello",
   "texto": [
    "**Olá** is good for everyone.",
    "According to the time: **bom dia** (until eating time), **boa tarde** (until dark) and **boa noite** (at night, also to greet).",
    "To say goodbye: **adeus** or **até logo** (see you later)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "You, you and the forms of treatment",
   "texto": [
    "**Tu** is used with people of trust; its distribution also varies by region and relationship.",
    "For formal treatment, **o senhor** and **a senhora** are clear, with the verb in third person.",
    "**Você** exists in Portugal, but its social value depends on the area and context; it does not always amount to a neutral «You». If you doubt, you can use **o senhor / a senhora** or a courteous question without explicit pronoun.",
    "To say your name: **Chamo-me Ana** or **Eu sou a Ana**. In Portugal the article with family-speaking first names (**o Pedro, a Ana**) is very common, but it is not mandatory: **Sou Ana** is also correct.",
    "To ask: **Como te chamas?** (you) or **Como se chama?** (formal treatment)."
   ]
  },
